  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "high",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "The design exhibits a complete Lethal Trifecta (TC1) attack path where an untrusted inbound email can manipulate the agent into reading arbitrary customer records and exfiltrating them via outbound email. The lack of scoped credentials and human approval makes the inherent risk critical. Only a behavioral prompt instruction restrains this capability, resulting in a high residual risk that is likely to become critical upon model upgrade."
  },
  "limitations": [
